    "english":  "The black crow perches upon the withered neem branch\nand caws toward the east, announcing the arrival of guests.\nMy left eye twitches with a sweet omen of joy,\nand the golden beauty-spots on my breast seem to glow anew.\nSurely he has crossed the dry stony hills and completed his quest;\nthe soft northern breeze begins to whisper across our terrace,\nbringing the scent of the first seasonal blooms.\nGrief will flee from this home, and the slender golden bangles\nthat slipped from my wasting arms will once again fit tight!",
